  "raw_text": "Sec. 8. A7id be it furjher enacted. That whenever the President of the United States shall have reason to believe that offenses have been or are likelj' to bo committed against the provisions of this act within any judicial district, it shall be lawful for him, in his discretion, to direct the judge, marshal, and district attorney of such district to attend at such place witiiin the district, and for such time as he may designate, for the purpose of the more speedy arrest and trial of persons charged with a violation of this act: and it shall be the duty of every Judge or other officer, when any such requisition shall be received by him, to attend at the place and for the time therein desig- nated.",
